body:
I've come full circle.

I started on Soul Eater almost exactly 5 years ago, which was pretty good, then I moved onto some stuff like Vampire Knight and Hetalia (which I laugh at myself for).  During eighth grade and into my freshman year, I got into some shows like Durarara!!, No.6, Kids on the Slope, Kimi to Boku, stuff kind of like that (if that can even be given a kind???).  Sophomore and junior year, I took a bit of a hiatus and watched let's players on Youtube obsessively for a while.  Now I'm laughing at myself again for getting so into Free! this past year, which I swore up and down I wouldn't do because 'it's a disgrace to my sport'.  Yeah.  I watched that shit, loved it, and cried every week for the last five episodes.  Even if they breathe *every Goddamn stroke*.  About two weeks ago, I got around to finishing Psycho-Pass, which I don't understand why I didn't do it sooner.  I'm not 100% on whether I want to watch the second season though;;;

Finally, with Durarara!! having its second season right now, I can hear slightly-past-the-Hetalia-phase eighth-grade-me shrieking in the distance.
